# go-api

Go server for the portal's machine-only endpoints. The Apps Script syncs and the CleverTap webhook call these; no agent screen does. Paths, secrets, request bodies and responses match the Next.js routes they replace, so moving a script over only means changing the host in its URL property.

| Endpoint | Caller |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/internal/sub-raw-onboarding-sync` | `scripts/sub-raw-onboarding-sync.gs` |
| `POST /api/internal/csm-sync` | `scripts/csm-sync.gs` |
| `POST /api/admin/merchant-sync` | `docs/google-sheets-merchant-sync.gs` |
| `POST /api/internal/leadgen-sync` | `scripts/leadgen-sync.gs` |
| `POST /api/internal/ad-conversions-sync` | `scripts/ad-conversions-sync.gs` |
| `POST /api/internal/ct-payment` | CleverTap webhook |
| `GET /healthz` | uptime checks |

Two things work differently from Next.js:

- **The 8:30 AM backlog rebalance** runs on the server's own 5-minute clock (once at boot, then every 5 minutes) instead of riding on the lead sync. The `daily_jobs` claim still limits it to one run a day.
- **WhatsApp sending stays in Next.js**, so templates and send rules live only in `lib/wa.ts`. After a CSM sync or a lead sync, this server calls `POST /api/internal/wa-run` on Next.js.

The roster rotation, lead linking and CSM queue rules are now in both codebases. A change to `lib/onboarding.ts`, `lib/leadgen.ts`, `lib/csm.ts`, `lib/ct.ts` or `lib/onboarding-rebalance.ts` has to be made here too.

## Run

```sh
go test ./...
[redacted] [redacted] [redacted] [redacted] \
NEXT_BASE_URL=https://pi-commerce-call-center-disposition.vercel.app go run .
```

| Env | |
|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Neon pooled connection string, the same database as Next.js |
| `SUB_RAW_SYNC_SECRET` | Sub Raw, CSM, lead gen and ad conversion syncs, plus the call to `wa-run` |
| `CT_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | CleverTap webhook |
| `MERCHANT_SYNC_SECRET` | Merchant sync |
| `MERCHANT_SYNC_MIN_ROWS` | Optional, default 100 |
| `NEXT_BASE_URL` | Next.js host for `wa-run`. If unset, WhatsApp jobs are skipped and logged |
| `PORT` | Default 8080 |

Deploy it as a long-running service in the same region as the database (Mumbai after the move). It is a single static binary: `go build -o go-api .`

## Cutover

1. Deploy, then check that `/healthz` returns `ok`.
2. Move one script at a time: point its URL property at this server and check its next run in the script's log. Start with ad conversions, then merchant, lead gen, Sub Raw, CSM, and CleverTap last.
3. Once a few days pass without errors, delete the Next.js route for each moved endpoint. Keep the `GET` in `ct-payment`, which is the admin view, and keep `wa-run`.

Running both servers at once is safe. Each sync takes the same advisory locks, CleverTap retries match on the same `dedupe_key`, and the rebalance is claimed once a day.
---
import { timingSafeEqual } from 'crypto';
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { db } from '@/lib/db';
import { ensureCsmWaRun,retryOnboardingNoPhone } from '@/lib/wa';

// WhatsApp jobs for the Go sync server (go-api), which hands sending back here so the templates
// and send rules stay in lib/wa.ts only:
//   csm                  after a completed CSM sync (T1–T5 on the fresh snapshot)
//   onboarding-no-phone  after each 5-minute lead sync (yesterday's no-phone onboarding messages)
// Same secret as the Sub Raw / CSM syncs.
function sameSecret(a:string,b:string){const aa=Buffer.from(a),bb=Buffer.from(b);return aa.length===bb.length&&timingSafeEqual(aa,bb);}

export const maxDuration=300;

export async function POST(req:Request){
  const configured=process.env.SUB_RAW_SYNC_SECRET||'';
  const supplied=req.headers.get('x-sub-raw-sync-secret')||'';
  if(!configured||!supplied||!sameSecret(configured,supplied)) return NextResponse.json({error:'Unauthorized'},{status:401});
  const body:any=await req.json().catch(()=>null);
  const sql=db();
  if(body?.job==='csm'){ await ensureCsmWaRun(sql); return NextResponse.json({ok:true}); }
  if(body?.job==='onboarding-no-phone') return NextResponse.json({ok:true,sent:await retryOnboardingNoPhone(sql)});
  return NextResponse.json({error:'Unknown job'},{status:400});
}

